  "notes": "West leads the ♠2 against 7♠. West's opening trump lead is won by South. The only possible loser is the ♦2. If one of the defenders has 5 or more diamonds, South must find a way of disposing of this loser.\n\nSouth should begin by cashing a second round of trump. If spades prove to be 2-2, the ♦2 can be safely trumped in the dummy.\n\nIf a defender discards on the second round of trump, South must proceed with caution. Cashing a third round of trump will leave South dependent on a favourable break in diamonds. Playing on diamonds instead will risk defeat if the defender with the remaining trump also has a singleton diamond.\n\nSouth should cash his top hearts, discarding a diamond from dummy on the second round. After cashing one top diamond, South can play the ♦2 and trump it in the dummy. As North and South have all of the high trumps, an overruff is not a danger.\n\nSouth can play a club from dummy and trump it. The last trump can be drawn and South's hand is high.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠2 against 7♠. West's opening trump lead is won by South. The only possible loser is the ♦2. If one of the defenders has 5 or more diamonds, South must find a way of disposing of this loser.",
